# BPMN 2.0's drawable vocabulary, one row per glyph, each either spent or withheld with a reason.
# The set of glyphs is a closed list fixed by an outside authority, so this is the boundary of
# what this model claims, stated as data instead of as prose.
#
# A `VALUES` literal
#   For `diagrams/graphs.sqlc`'s reason. Everything else that checks the emission is worked out from
#   the emission: `examples/diagramming` reads the element kinds off disk and asks whether each is
#   governed. That can report an element this repository drew and never decided about. It can never
#   report an element BPMN has and this repository ignored, because an unused glyph leaves no trace
#   in the artifact to be read. The unused half of the notation cannot be reached from the
#   artifact, so it has to be declared.
#
# What could not be drawn is listed
#   It is the only way to meet what this emission owes: what could not be drawn must be listed,
#   because from outside a blank diagram and a diagram of nothing look the same. The set of glyphs
#   is the list. Without it, "gateways are not drawn here" and "gateways were forgotten" are the
#   same sentence.
#
# Exactly one of the two is filled
#   Exactly one of `stands_for` and `withheld_because` is filled, the schema's own `<>` idiom in a
#   roster. A fact or a typed reason there is none, never a blank and never both. A glyph with
#   neither is the finding: it means somebody moved a row and did not say why.
#
# `withheld_because` holds four kinds of reason
#   It is not one reason in forty disguises, and reading it that way is how the boundary gets
#   restated as "out of scope". Four different things are in this column: a routing element, which
#   BPMN owns and this model leaves to it; a performer element nothing can fill, because the
#   claimant graph files no edges; a data element refused because it would appear to carry a figure
#   it cannot hold; and an element that is an open question rather than a settled no.
#
# The fourth kind is empty
#   `group` is not in it. A group carries no membership of its own; `tFlowElement/categoryValueRef`
#   does, and it is `maxOccurs="unbounded"`. A roster organised by region cannot find that, because
#   BPMN files the glyph under artifacts and the mechanism in the semantic core, so listing the
#   artifact region reads "purely visual" and stops. A fact whose glyph and whose mechanism sit in
#   different regions cannot be seen by a list organised by region, and this roster is one.
#
# The diagram interchange is part of the vocabulary
#   The roster covers BPMN's `BPMNDI.xsd` as well as `Semantic.xsd`. The DI half is the half about
#   drawing, and `bpmndi:BPMNDiagram` sits in `tDefinitions`'s own sequence: the document has a
#   place set aside for its picture. A roster checked against `Semantic.xsd` alone would miss every
#   DI element while calling itself BPMN's closed drawable vocabulary.
-- BPMN 2.0 §7 (activities), §8 (gateways, events), §9 (swimlanes), §10 (data), §11 (artifacts).
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
# Activities. The three this emission spends, and the border is what tells them apart.
  ('task'::text, 'rounded rectangle, thin border'::text, 'composition'::text, true,
   'pm:Operation, reached by ForeignId'::text, NULL::text),
  ('callActivity', 'rounded rectangle, thick border', 'composition', true,
   'asrt:Part crossing a document. The thick border is the notation for substitution, so this glyph is what a compose directive renders as, and drawing it like a task discards the pipeline', NULL),
  ('subProcess', 'rounded rectangle with the ⊞ marker', 'composition', false,
   NULL, 'A local fusion drawn as this says the wrong thing twice: a subProcess is an activity '
         'inside a lane, where a fusion''s parts divide a layer among them, and it is a flow '
         'node, so it leaves layer grain exactly as a callActivity does. `childLaneSet` says the '
         'true thing and stays keyed (filing, layer). Withheld on the composition axis, which the '
         'ceded law refuses outright, so it is legible only through diagrams/admitted.sqlc'),
  ('childLaneSet', 'a laneSet nested inside one lane', 'composition', true,
   'A fusion''s parts divide what they compose among them, and a lane nested inside a lane '
   'draws that division. A nested lane is still keyed (filing, layer), so unlike a call it '
   'collapses nothing and can invent nothing', NULL),
  ('transaction', 'double-bordered rounded rectangle', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'a rollback boundary, and nothing here can be undone. A remainder is an accounting fact and not an effect, so there is no state to restore'),
  ('adHocSubProcess', 'rounded rectangle with the ~ marker', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'The near miss. The tilde declares its children have no required order, and siblings '
         'here genuinely have none. But the composition does order them: a layer is worked out '
         'after every part beneath it, and a jagged layer is exactly where that order and the '
         'depth part ways. Drawing this would erase the one order this model has'),
  ('userTask', 'rounded rectangle, person marker', 'performer', false,
   NULL, 'a subtype names who performs, and the performer is the claimant graph, which has no table and files no edges. Emitting one would guess an attribution nothing filed'),
  ('serviceTask', 'rounded rectangle, gear marker', 'performer', false,
   NULL, 'the claimant graph again, and this is the row EU review turns on: software and an AI agent are both claimants here and BPMN spells both as this one glyph'),
  ('manualTask', 'rounded rectangle, hand marker', 'performer', false, NULL, 'the claimant graph: no edges filed'),
  ('scriptTask', 'rounded rectangle, script marker', 'performer', false, NULL, 'the claimant graph: no edges filed'),
  ('businessRuleTask', 'rounded rectangle, table marker', 'performer', false,
   NULL, 'nearest to a regime citation, and wrong: a rule task is a node that evaluates a rule, where pm.regime is the authority a figure is filed under'),
  ('sendTask', 'rounded rectangle, filled envelope', 'routing', false, NULL, 'a message, and there is no token to carry one'),
  ('receiveTask', 'rounded rectangle, open envelope', 'routing', false, NULL, 'a message, and there is no token to carry one'),
  ('performer', 'none, an attribute of an activity', 'performer', false,
   NULL, 'The element the claimant graph would use, and the reason it is empty. Delegation is a '
         'claimant-to-claimant edge and nothing in the schema files one, so this is a slot with '
         'no filler rather than a refusal'),

# Gateways. One reason, five glyphs: the largest single region of the notation, and all of it is
# routing, which BPMN owns and this model leaves to it.
  ('exclusiveGateway', 'diamond with an X', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'BPMN owns what happens next and under what condition. There is no token here to route'),
  ('parallelGateway', 'diamond with a +', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'routing. And a fusion is not this: a fusion sums a carrier, a parallel gateway splits '
         'a token'),
  ('inclusiveGateway', 'diamond with an O', 'routing', false, NULL, 'routing'),
  ('eventBasedGateway', 'diamond with a pentagon', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'routing, and it needs events'),
  ('complexGateway', 'diamond with an asterisk', 'routing', false, NULL, 'routing'),

# Events. The start and end rows are the ones that carry an argument.
  ('startEvent', 'thin circle', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'The expansion owes a start and an end, and the composition has them by having a root '
         'and having leaves, so no element is needed for them. A startEvent is where a token '
         'enters, which is a different claim'),
  ('endEvent', 'thick circle', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'the leaves of the composition are the end, and composition/leaves.sqlc counts them'),
  ('intermediateCatchEvent', 'double circle', 'routing', false, NULL, 'no token, no clock'),
  ('intermediateThrowEvent', 'double circle, filled marker', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'no token, no clock'),
  ('boundaryEvent', 'double circle on an activity edge', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'an interruption is a control-flow event'),
  ('timerEventDefinition', 'clock face', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'There is no clock here, and a window is not one. pm:window is a calendar extent: it '
         'says over what span a figure was measured, never when anything fires'),
  ('messageEventDefinition', 'envelope', 'routing', false, NULL, 'no token'),
  ('errorEventDefinition', 'lightning bolt', 'routing', false, NULL, 'Not a violation. A check reports a contradiction between filed sentences; an error event is a runtime throw'),
  ('signalEventDefinition', 'triangle', 'routing', false, NULL, 'no token'),
  ('escalationEventDefinition', 'open arrowhead', 'routing', false, NULL, 'no token'),
  ('compensateEventDefinition', 'rewind marker', 'routing', false, NULL, 'compensation undoes an effect, and an elimination corrects a count. Nothing is undone here'),
  ('conditionalEventDefinition', 'lined page', 'routing', false, NULL, 'no token'),
  ('terminateEventDefinition', 'filled circle', 'routing', false, NULL, 'no token'),
  ('linkEventDefinition', 'arrow', 'routing', false, NULL, 'no token'),

# Connectors. One carried and the rest refused, and one refusal is a named trap.
  ('sequenceFlow', 'solid line, filled arrowhead', 'routing', false,
   NULL, 'The composition is a call graph and not sequence flow, and BPMN has both. Drawing the '
         'composition as sequence flow claims an execution order the model never states'),
  ('messageFlow', 'dashed line, open arrowhead', 'collaboration', false,
   NULL, 'The named trap: a coupling is not a message flow. Drawing one as the other reads '
         'pm:Layer''s word *independently* as control-flow independence, when the schema''s test '
         'is co-movement. A pool''s independence is about tokens; a layer''s is about accounting'),
  ('association', 'dotted line with an open arrowhead', 'artifact', true,
   'pm:Coupling, the observation that can show the model wrong. What an association is for is '
   'attaching a textAnnotation; what it can hold is wider: `tAssociation` extends `tArtifact` '
   'with `sourceRef` and `targetRef` as required unconstrained QNames, so it is a general typed '
   'edge and two lanes are a legal pair. `associationDirection="One"` because a coupling has a '
   'direction and every consumer reads it; BPMN glosses an arrowhead as a direction of flow and '
   'a coupling is a dependence, which is safe only because the composition is drawn as '
   'containment and this is the only line in the emitted notation. Drawing the composition as '
   'an edge would reopen this choice', NULL),
  ('dataAssociation', 'dotted line, open arrowhead', 'data', false,
   NULL, 'Refused on its content model and not on its usual job. Two refusals, both about this element: `sourceRef` and `targetRef` are `xsd:IDREF`, so it cannot cross a document where `tAssociation`''s QNames can. And its `transformation` is a `tFormalExpression`, which is single valued, where every quantity here is three points. That is the sharper form of *BPMN carries no quantity*: it carries one, and a claim is an interval'),

# Swimlanes. Spent but for one attribute BPMN has and this model leaves empty, and the black box
# is the one that pays twice.
  ('participant', 'pool: a labelled band', 'collaboration', true,
   'a filing. And with no processRef it is a black box, which is first-class BPMN for *a party acts here and what they do is not in this diagram*: the unfilled @scope slot, drawn', NULL),
  ('lane', 'a band subdividing a pool', 'composition', true, 'pm:Layer, and the region it delimits', NULL),
  ('partitionElementRef', 'none, an attribute of a lane', 'composition', false,
   NULL, 'A slot with no filler, and the only place BPMN is the finer of the two. `tLane` '
         'carries this and `partitionElement` for what the lanes are divided by, per lane, where '
         'this model files one `Scope/basis` per stack. The nearest filler is the absorber '
         'buffer, and it does not fit: several layers of one filing can share one buffer, so '
         'pointing at it would assert a division the model does not make. A layer''s identity is '
         'its name and nothing else, so there is no element to point at. The same state as '
         '`performer`, reached from the opposite direction'),
  ('laneSet', 'none, it is the subdivision', 'composition', true, 'pm:Stack, a partition claimed exhaustive', NULL),

# The cover: the inductions, whose element sits in a different region of the standard.
  ('categoryValueRef', 'none, it is drawn by a group', 'composition', true,
   'pm:Induction, and the element that makes the inductions drawable at all. `tFlowElement` '
   'carries it with `maxOccurs="unbounded"`, so a flow node may be in many categories where '
   '`flowNodeRef` puts it in one lane. The draws are a containment and the inductions a cover, '
   'and the direction is reversed: a lane collects its members, a categoryValue collects nobody '
   'and the member declares the tie', NULL),
  ('categoryValue', 'none, the group''s label', 'composition', true,
   'a layer that some operation induces into, and it carries the name and not a reference. `tCategoryValue` extends `tBaseElement` and adds one `xs:string`, so the layer arrives as text beside a `lane` of the same name with nothing tying them. The weaker cousin of the callActivity defect: a call loses the layer, this loses only the pointer', NULL),
  ('category', 'none, a rootElement under definitions', 'composition', true,
   'the classification scheme the inductions make, one per document that has an induction to '
   'classify. A rootElement, so it is QName addressable across documents even though nothing '
   'crosses one yet', NULL),

# Data. The closest BPMN comes to this model's actual subject, and refused for that reason.
  ('dataObject', 'rectangle with a folded corner', 'data', false,
   NULL, 'The one that looks like it fits: this glyph names what a routed operation takes and '
         'commits, which is this model''s subject. It carries a name and a state; a demand here is '
         'three points, a unit, a taxonomy and a typed absence. Emitting it would make the diagram '
         'appear to carry a magnitude it cannot hold, which is the analyst failure exactly, and a '
         'composed layer''s figures stay off the drawing for the same reason'),
  ('dataStore', 'cylinder', 'data', false, NULL, 'persistence, which no filing claims'),
  ('dataInput', 'rectangle, folded corner, open arrow', 'data', false, NULL, 'the dataObject argument, at the activity boundary'),
  ('dataOutput', 'rectangle, folded corner, filled arrow', 'data', false, NULL, 'the dataObject argument, at the activity boundary'),

# Artifacts. `group` is the glyph that draws the inductions.
  ('group', 'dashed rounded rectangle', 'artifact', true,
   'A glyph and not a fact. A group is to `categoryValueRef` what a `lane` is to '
   '`flowNodeRef`: the drawn shape of a membership held on the members. It implies no '
   'containment because the membership it draws permits many parents, which is why the '
   'inductions fit it and the draws do not. It carries `pm:Induction`, and without it the '
   'categoryValueRefs are readable and invisible', NULL),
  ('textAnnotation', 'open bracket with text', 'artifact', true,
   'The only element in BPMN that puts words on the canvas. A `documentation` attaches to an '
   'element where this floats beside one, and a `documentation` is invisible in every rendering '
   'where this is not. `diagrams/legends.sqlc` is the population, and a fact carried in '
   '`documentation` alone is in the artifact and on no page. Emitted floating, with no '
   '`association`, because attaching it would spend that element a second way, and the '
   'association already carries the coupling lines', NULL),
  ('text', 'the annotation''s words', 'artifact', true, 'the note itself, and `tTextAnnotation` carries a `textFormat` this emitter leaves at its default', NULL),

# Infrastructure. No glyph, and the last row is the whole boundary in one element.
  ('definitions', 'none', 'infrastructure', true, 'the document, and targetNamespace is the filing identity', NULL),
  ('collaboration', 'none', 'infrastructure', true, 'the container the pool lives in', NULL),
  ('process', 'none, it is the pool''s contents', 'composition', true, 'a composition, one .sqlc, an ad-hoc view never built', NULL),
  ('import', 'none', 'infrastructure', true, 'Derived, never declared: the cross-document references. An identity table is a targetNamespace and not an import', NULL),
  ('documentation', 'none', 'infrastructure', true,
   'the evaluation order and the provenance, as untyped text that carries the words and not '
   'the claim', NULL),
  ('flowNodeRef', 'none', 'composition', true, 'lane membership, which is the orphan law', NULL),
  ('relationship', 'none, it is not drawn at all', 'infrastructure', true,
   'the composition at layer grain, and it sits on the same shelf as the row below it on '
   'purpose. Both are BPMN''s extensibility, and they are refused and spent for the same test '
   'applied to two different content models: `tRelationship` carries two QNames and a required '
   '`type` string, so it names positions in another document and imports nothing, which is '
   'what ForeignId does. Not a glyph: no diagram shows it, so this promotes the fact for a tool '
   'and leaves the reader the callActivity name they already had', NULL),
  ('source', 'none', 'infrastructure', true, 'the composed layer end of a relationship, as a QName into this document', NULL),
  ('target', 'none', 'infrastructure', true, 'the part end, as a QName into an imported document. The thing `calledElement` cannot do: a QName there must name a CallableElement and a lane is not one, and the XSD would accept it anyway, which is well-formed and wrong', NULL),
# The diagram interchange, the half of BPMN that is about drawing.
  ('BPMNDiagram', 'none, it is the container of the picture', 'interchange', true,
   'The SVG''s proper place in the document. A document with no plane leaves the SVG stage to derive its geometry from nothing, inventing coordinates, and a cache whose content has no original is a second opinion rather than a cache', NULL),
  ('BPMNPlane', 'none, the surface the shapes sit on', 'interchange', true,
   'the collaboration, drawn. One plane per document, naming the element the picture is of', NULL),
  ('BPMNShape', 'none, it places a glyph', 'interchange', true,
   'the box of every element that gets one: a pool, a lane, a flow node, a group and a text '
   'annotation. Filing a coordinate in a relation is what `diagrams/shapes.sqlc` refuses, while '
   'deriving one into the artifact is what the emitter does for every box here. An element '
   'with no shape is an element every reader but the renderer beside it loses, and loses '
   'without an error', NULL),
  ('Bounds', 'none, x/y/width/height', 'interchange', true,
   'the geometry itself, from the DC namespace. The one place in this pipeline where a number is legitimately drawn, because it is a coordinate and not a magnitude', NULL),
  ('BPMNEdge', 'none, it routes a connector', 'interchange', true,
   'The coupling line''s route, and it is the only edge in the notation. It places a `sequenceFlow`, a `messageFlow`, an `association` or a `dataAssociation`, and of those only `association` is spent here, so an edge in one of these documents is a dependence and can be nothing else. Four `di:waypoint`s describe the gutter run, which is what keeps the line outside both lanes', NULL),
  ('waypoint', 'none, a point on a route', 'interchange', true,
   'a corner of an edge, from the DI namespace proper rather than from `bpmndi` or `dc`. An edge could not be given a route without it, which is why the emitter declares a third namespace', NULL),
  ('BPMNLabel', 'none, it places a label', 'interchange', false,
   NULL, 'where a shape''s text sits. Every label here is placed relative to its own box by one rule, so filing a position per label would be filing what a rule already determines'),
  ('BPMNLabelStyle', 'none, a font', 'interchange', false,
   NULL, 'typography, and the SVG carries one stylesheet. The one DI element that is purely presentational, so it is the only refusal in this block that is about taste rather than derivation'),

  ('extensionElements', 'none', 'infrastructure', false,
   NULL, 'The escape hatch, and refusing it is the boundary. Taking it would put this model inside a BPMN document rather than beside it. ForeignId crosses by naming a position in the other document and never by importing any of it, and an extension element is importing all of it')
) AS n(element, glyph, axis, emitted, stands_for, withheld_because)
